> det [[1, 2], [3, 4]] mod 7
the 2x2 matrix over GF(7)
  [1 2]
  [3 4]
  det = 5
  how: Gaussian elimination mod p, the product of the pivots
> det [[1, 2], [3, 4]] mod 2
the 2x2 matrix over GF(2)
  [1 0]
  [1 0]
  det = 0
  how: Gaussian elimination mod p, the product of the pivots
> det [[1, 2], [3, 4]] mod 4
the 2x2 matrix over Z/4
  [1 2]
  [3 0]
  det = 2 (not a unit)
  how: row reduction by Euclid's algorithm on each column (only swaps and row subtractions, which keep the determinant up to sign)
